========
Herwig 7
========

This is the release of Herwig 7.3.0, a multi purpose event
generator for high energy physics.

The Herwig++ distribution contains an adapted version of LoopTools 2.6
<http://www.feynarts.de/looptools/>. 

BUILD AND INSTALL
=================
Please refer to https://herwig.hepforge.org/tutorials/ for detailed 
instructions.

The LEP-BeamSpread.in example uses ThePEG::GaussianBeamLuminosity from the
standard ThePEG library. It is installed alongside LEP.in and runs with
'Herwig read LEP-BeamSpread.in' followed by 'Herwig run LEP-BeamSpread.run'.
The example selects 45.6 GeV per beam and independent 0.221% energy spreads.
Build and install ThePEG before Herwig when updating the luminosity interface.
This branch requires a rebuild against ThePEG ABI 31:0:0. Matchbox's
IdentifiedParticleCut and PairRapidityCut now include the beam rapidity in
laboratory selections, including the pair pseudorapidity option. This changes
asymmetric fixed-beam setups such as DIS as well as Gaussian-spread runs.
Their native regression is included in 'make check'.

The LEP-DecayCylinder.in, LEP-FCC-DecayCylinder.in, LEP-VertexSmearing.in,
LEP-BeamSpread-Geometry.in and LEP-EvtGenGeometry.in examples use the built-in geometry controls. Cylinder
restrictions and Gaussian vertex/time smearing are independent and default to
off. EvtGen lifetime ownership is separately opt-in; LegacyHerwig remains the
default. These options require StandardEventHandler. LHE input and decays
performed inside the shower/hard process are outside the cylinder scope.
See each card for explicit species choices and native/EvtGen decay tables.
LEP-FCC-DecayCylinder.in selects only s sbar with ISR at 91.188 GeV;
LEP-DecayCylinder.in is the five-flavour geometry example without ISR.
FCC-ee.in combines all three new features: independent 0.221% beam spreads,
FCC vertex/time widths and the 2250/2500 mm laboratory cylinder. It selects
s sbar at 91.188 GeV with lepton ISR, QCD/QED final-state radiation and native
decays. It explicitly enables smearing, which is off in the FCC reference
Pythia card. Run 'Herwig read FCC-ee.in', then 'Herwig run FCC-ee.run';
the default is 100000 events, or use '-N 1000' for a quick check.
In the opt-in EvtGen lifetime model, a rejected decay discards the event
without retry, independently of output redirection. LegacyHerwig's complete
tree path continues to use EvtGen's original entry point.
After adding geometry to this unreleased ABI 31 branch, clean-rebuild ThePEG,
Herwig and all dependent modules, and recreate saved runs.
